  heading="How to find the volume and area of any shape"
  updated="2026-10-01"
>
  <p slot="intro" class="guide-intro">Volume is the space inside a solid, in cubic units. Area is the space inside a flat shape, in square units. Both come from a few measurements and one formula per shape. This guide gives each formula with a worked example. To skip the arithmetic, use the <a href={volume}>volume calculator</a> or the <a href={area}>area calculator</a>.</p>

